<title>HONG KONG: Shougang Grand 1996 net returns to gain.</title>
<headline>Shougang Grand 1996 net returns to gain.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   17.32 gain    vs 8.23 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    2.0	     vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  76.15 gain    vs 106.70 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    115.88 profit vs 54.70 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     77.83	   vs 91.60</p>
<p>    Company name		 Shougang Concord Grand (Group) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 5-12</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Shougang Concord Grand is involved in property development, finance and strategic investments.</p>
<p>The company proposed a special dividend of 0.50 H.K. cents per share vs nil.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$33.32 million on translation of convertible notes net of hedging premium, gain of HK$57.15 million on disposal of investment properties and loss of HK$14.32 million on provision for premium on early redemption of convertible notes.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 2.5 H.K. cents (including special dividend) vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
